cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hydrocal in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "hydrocal: hydrogenic atomic structure calculations and radiative transition rates"
type: software
abstract: >-
  hydrocal is a collection of subroutines performing hydrogenic atomic
  structure calculations such as bound-bound and bound-free radiative
  transition rates, which are then used, for example, in the calculation of
  cross sections and rate coefficients for radiative recombination.
